				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-399227#post-3705125</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-399227/scp-1234-j#post-3705125</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 09 Feb 2018 04:22:57 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DeRockProject</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>486453</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I think everyone is doing this joke wrong. Instead of how previous comments have worded their comments, I believe this is how you are supposed to do it. This is how you are supposed to do it.</p> <p>&#8230;</p> <p>I am familiar with this author's SCPs to a degree that may or may not be zero, and was expecting similar quality from this article.</p> <p>This article is of a quality. I give it a vote. The amount of the vote is -1, 0, or 1, no more or less. It's narrative existed and the image was present. The image does not break copyright laws. This article existed for a period of time and it represents its era of the SCP-wiki to an extent.</p> <p>The audio extracted an emotion out of me. This SCP makes me feel an emotion. I fear or empathize with an aspect of it.</p> <p>I'd like to suggest a crosslink. It is a crosslink. It will change your article from an article to an article. Collapsible.</p> <p>I feel like you could've wrote the article better. I also feel it could've been worse. I should say your article made me laugh. Or I could lie.</p> <p>wait, what am I doing anymore?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
